WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.520
You learned what changes when a script
leaves Graph for Resource Manager:

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.022
another host and token, Azure
role-based access control

4
00:00:09.022 --> 00:00:12.525
instead of a permission list,
api-versions, and next link.

5
00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:15.453
You paged Resource Graph
without losing rows,

6
00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:19.613
and saw when it can't page and why
an empty result can mean no access.

7
00:00:19.613 --> 00:00:24.676
You read the Arc machine, extension,
SQL Server, policy assignment and policy

8
00:00:24.676 --> 00:00:29.663
state records, and checked support dates
against Microsoft's lifecycle pages.

9
00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:34.096
And in Lab 1 you ran the five checks
on fixtures in Python and PowerShell,

10
00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:36.725
and read each finding against its control.

11
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:40.998
That finishes the Microsoft Automation
learning path as it stands:

12
00:00:40.998 --> 00:00:44.737
four modules, about five hours
and fifty-five minutes in all.

13
00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:48.074
To put the checks on a schedule,
go to the Azure Arc track

14
00:00:48.074 --> 00:00:51.337
implementation guide's Step
8, and its Gate 8 checks it.

15
00:00:51.337 --> 00:00:54.385
Modules on Teams Phone
and Teams administration,

16
00:00:54.385 --> 00:00:57.120
and on monitoring and
evidence, are planned.
